# forjar 1.31.0 cut — the reds, and what cleared each

Every red below was cleared BEFORE the commit `make dogfood-release` then
measured, which is why the run itself is nine-for-nine on its first attempt.
The reds are recorded here because a gate that was never red proves nothing
about itself.

### RED — gate H, before the crux rows matched the keys it greps
GATE H FAIL 3 behaviour bullet(s) under [1.31.0] have no row in docs/audits/crux-1.31.0.md — the rows above are the keys each must contain
  forjar drift declines — exit 2,
  A service is converged only while
  forjar drift exits 1 on any

The rows existed. They read `| (1) \`forjar drift\` declines — exit 2, …`, and
`crux_row()` greps the bullet's first six words as a FIXED string: "forjar drift
declines — exit 2, the" does not occur in "`forjar drift` declines". The
backticks came out of the key span.

### GREEN — gate H
GATE H PASS 3 of 3 behaviour bullet(s) under [1.31.0] reconciled in docs/audits/crux-1.31.0.md, each naming >= 3 of the 28 surveyed systems

