### GREEN — after the repair, measured on the committed tree by the gate itself
GATE B PASS comply clean; ruleset 13878864 requires [gate]; 14 gate script(s) and 4 other tracked script(s) at 0 bashrs errors; ratchet CB-200 held; ratchet CB-2110=49/49 CB-2111=49/49 CB-2112=34/35 CB-2114=34/34 CB-2115=42/43 held; required check(s) [gate] reach a dogfood gate; legacy bashrs errors 1 <= 1

### the composition, measured either side (pmat comply check)
before: CB-2112 37 (NO-ISSUE 24, TAIL-MISMATCH 10, ISSUE-CLOSED 3); CB-2114 36 NO-RELEASE; CB-2115 49 (ORPHAN-ROADMAP 27, ORPHAN-GITHUB 11, DRIFT 11)
after:  CB-2112 34 (NO-ISSUE 24, TAIL-MISMATCH 10);                 CB-2114 34 NO-RELEASE; CB-2115 42 (ORPHAN-ROADMAP 24, ORPHAN-GITHUB  8, DRIFT 10)

CB-2114's repair is two rows, not four: PMAT-560 gained `release: 1.31.0`, and
PMAT-574's own row was minted without one and then given `release: 1.31.0`. The
three rows minted for #565, #572 and #573 were each created WITH
`release: 1.32.0`, so they added no NO-RELEASE finding to remove. 36 - 2 = 34,
which is what the gate measured.

CB-2115 read 43 once, from `scripts/ratchets/comply-count.sh` against the
working tree at 05:00Z, and 42 every time since — gate B on the committed tree,
and a re-measurement at 06:40Z whose composition (24 + 8 + 10) sums to 42. The
first draft of this log explained the difference as "the receipts this commit
had not yet added", and a review lane refuted it: markdown receipts cannot move
ORPHAN-ROADMAP, ORPHAN-GITHUB or DRIFT. What is true is narrower and worth
more: `pmat comply` reads GitHub LIVE and stamps each run with its own
`snapshot: gh paiml/forjar taken <ts>`, so two runs minutes apart are two
measurements of a moving source, and the composition that SUMS is the one to
trust. No ceiling is lowered here in any case: a ceiling may only be lowered
from a measurement of the COMMITTED tree, and the tree that carries these
numbers is the one the next commit makes.

### REFUSED — the commit-msg hook, on the first attempt at the cut commit
PMAT commit-msg: Pmat-Ticket PMAT-574 is completed — work belongs to an open item, and CB-2113 refuses this commit in CI.
  leave a ticket open in its own PR; the next ticket's PR marks it completed

The row said `completed` because the cut is what completes it. The hook is
right and the rule is the one the 1.30.0 loop already used: PMAT-555 was marked
completed by PMAT-557's booking PR, not by its own. PMAT-574 stays `inprogress`
here and the booking PR closes it.
